A thread destroyed while others lend it their time leaves them lending to memory that holds no thread.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a thread lends to something that is not another live thread

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -846,7 +846,7 @@ bool sched_forget(struct obj_header *o, bool preempt)
          * A thread that lends it its time named it in its call, which can no longer be answered.
          * Its progress is the ring: a stop leaves the rest lending to a thread still whole.
          */
-        while (t->lenders != 0) {
+        while (t->lenders != 0 && o->type != CAP_THREAD) {
             LOOP_PAID(sched_forget, waiter, "a thread that lent it its time, by a call of its own");
             struct thread *l = p2v(t->lenders);
             lend_remove(t, l);
